IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 1005 of 2022
CITATION: 2023 SCC OnLine SC 352
YEAR: 2023

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: S. Ravindra Bhat, Dipankar Datta

PARTIES:
Mohd Muslim vs State (NCT of Delhi)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, 1985, Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 37 NDPS, Article 21

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
undue delay, prolonged incarceration, speedy trial, bail in ndps

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that systemic delay in trial and prolonged incarceration of undertrials under the NDPS Act can supersede statutory limits of Section 37 to uphold Article 21.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 37 NDPS, Article 21.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

